[2026-03-16T01:41:16.238Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DcmuTr5rh25Ze7KxdjjkEP","type":"tool_result","content":"  1370→\n  1371→#### Test: Status dropdown can be changed multiple times\n  1372→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with Status \"Backlog\"\n  1373→- **Action**: User changes status to \"Todo\", then changes it to \"In Progress\", then back to \"Backlog\"\n  1374→- **Expected**: Status shows \"Backlog\" after the final change. Each intermediate state was correctly displayed.\n  1375→\n  1376→### CreateIssueActions\n  1377→\n  1378→#### Test: Create Issue button is visible and styled\n  1379→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1380→- **Expected**: A \"Create Issue\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal with primary styling (accent color background).\n  1381→\n  1382→#### Test: Cancel button is visible\n  1383→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1384→- **Expected**: A \"Cancel\" button is visible at the bottom of the modal alongside the \"Create Issue\" button.\n  1385→\n  1386→#### Test: Cancel button closes the modal\n  1387→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1388→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Cancel\" button\n  1389→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No issue is created. The user returns to the previous page view.\n  1390→\n  1391→#### Test: Cancel button discards form data\n  1392→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has entered title \"Draft issue\" and selected priority \"High\".\n  1393→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\", then opens the create issue modal again\n  1394→- **Expected**: The modal opens with all fields reset to defaults (empty title, Backlog status, No Priority). The previously entered data is not retained.\n  1395→\n  1396→#### Test: Create Issue button submits the form with all fields\n  1397→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. User has filled in: Title \"Implement OAuth\", Description \"Add OAuth support\", Status \"Todo\", Priority \"High\", Assignee \"Alice Smith\", Labels \"Feature\", Project \"API Redesign\", Cycle \"Sprint 10\", Due date \"Mar 25, 2026\".\n  1398→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1399→- **Expected**: The issue is created with all specified field values. A brief confirmation showing the new issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-43\") is displayed. The modal closes and the user is navigated to the issues list.\n  1400→\n  1401→#### Test: Create Issue with only required fields\n  1402→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with team \"Engineering\" selected\n  1403→- **Action**: User enters title \"Quick bug fix\" and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1404→- **Expected**: The issue is created with title \"Quick bug fix\", status \"Backlog\", priority \"No Priority\", and no assignee/labels/project/cycle/due date. The new issue identifier is briefly shown. The modal closes.\n  1405→\n  1406→#### Test: Created issue appears in the team issues list\n  1407→- **Initial state**: User is on Team Issues page for \"Engineering\". The page shows existing issues.\n  1408→- **Action**: User clicks \"New Issue\", enters title \"New feature request\", sets status to \"Todo\", and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1409→- **Expected**: After modal closes, the Team Issues list updates to include \"New feature request\" under the \"Todo\" status group with the correct issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-44\").\n  1410→\n  1411→#### Test: Created issue with parent appears as sub-issue\n  1412→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Issue \"ENG-1: Setup project\" exists.\n  1413→- **Action**: User enters title \"Write unit tests\", selects \"ENG-1: Setup project\" as parent issue, and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1414→- **Expected**: The issue is created. When navigating to \"ENG-1: Setup project\" detail page, \"Write unit tests\" appears in the sub-issues section.\n  1415→\n  1416→#### Test: Created issue generates activity history entry\n  1417→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1418→- **Action**: User creates an issue with title \"Track history\" and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1419→- **Expected**: When viewing the new issue's detail page, the Activity tab shows an initial \"created this issue\" entry with the current user's name and timestamp.\n  1420→\n  1421→#### Test: Created issue generates inbox notification for assignee\n  1422→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open. Current user is \"Alice Smith\".\n  1423→- **Action**: User creates an issue with title \"Review PR\", assigns it to \"Bob Jones\", and clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1424→- **Expected**: When Bob Jones checks their inbox, a notification appears: \"Alice Smith assigned you to [issue identifier]: Review PR\" with the correct timestamp. The inbox badge count increases.\n  1425→\n  1426→#### Test: Create Issue button is disabled during submission\n  1427→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open with valid data entered\n  1428→- **Action**: User clicks \"Create Issue\"\n  1429→- **Expected**: The \"Create Issue\" button becomes disabled (to prevent duplicate submissions) while the request is processing. It re-enables after the operation completes (success or failure).\n  1430→\n  1431→#### Test: Clicking outside the modal closes it\n  1432→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1433→- **Action**: User clicks on the overlay area outside the modal\n  1434→- **Expected**: The modal closes without creating an issue.\n  1435→\n  1436→#### Test: Pressing Escape closes the modal\n  1437→- **Initial state**: Create issue modal is open\n  1438→- **Action**: User presses the Escape key\n  1439→- **Expected**: The modal closes without creating an issue.\n  1440→\n  1441→#### Test: Creating multiple issues in sequence works correctly\n  1442→- **Initial state**: User is on Team Issues page for \"Engineering\"\n  1443→- **Action**: User creates issue \"First task\" via the modal, then opens the modal again and creates \"Second task\"\n  1444→- **Expected**: Both issues appear in the team issues list with sequential identifiers (e.g., \"ENG-43\", \"ENG-44\"). The modal resets correctly between creations.\n  1445→\n  1446→## Active Cycle Page (`/team/:teamId/cycles`)\n  1447→\n  1448→**Components**: CycleList, CycleDetail, CreateCycle, BurndownChart\n  1449→\n  1450→### CycleList\n  1451→\n  1452→#### Test: Cycle list renders all team cycles with name, date range, progress bar, and issue count\n  1453→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/team/eng-1/cycles`. The \"Engineering\" team has 3 cycles: \"Sprint 1\" (Jan 1–Jan 14, 8/10 issues done), \"Sprint 2\" (Jan 15–Jan 28, 3/8 issues done, active), \"Sprint 3\" (Jan 29–Feb 11, 0/5 issues done).\n  1454→- **Expected**: A list of 3 cycle rows is displayed. Each row shows the cycle name, date range (e.g., \"Jan 1 – Jan 14\"), a progress bar reflecting the completion percentage (e.g., 80% for Sprint 1), and the issue count (e.g., \"10 issues\"). Rows are ordered chronologically.\n  1455→\n  1456→#### Test: Active cycle is visually highlighted in the list\n  1457→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles`. \"Sprint 2\" is the active cycle.\n  1458→- **Expected**: The \"Sprint 2\" row has a distinct visual highlight (e.g., accent border, background color, or \"Active\" badge) that distinguishes it from the other cycles. Non-active cycles do not have this highlight.\n  1459→\n  1460→#### Test: Clicking a cycle navigates to cycle detail view\n  1461→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles` viewing the cycle list.\n  1462→- **Action**: User clicks on the \"Sprint 2\" cycle row.\n  1463→- **Expected**: The cycle detail view for \"Sprint 2\" is displayed, showing the cycle name, date range, progress stats, issue list, and burndown chart.\n  1464→\n  1465→#### Test: Cycle list shows empty state when team has no cycles\n  1466→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/team/design-1/cycles`. The \"Design\" team has no cycles.\n  1467→- **Expected**: An empty state message is displayed (e.g., \"No cycles yet. Create your first cycle to get started.\") with an icon. The \"New Cycle\" button is still visible.\n  1468→\n  1469→#### Test: Cycle list progress bar accurately reflects issue completion percentage\n  1470→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles`. \"Sprint 1\" has 8 of 10 issues done (80%), \"Sprint 2\" has 3 of 8 done (37.5%), \"Sprint 3\" has 0 of 5 done (0%).\n  1471→- **Expected**: Each cycle's progress bar width corresponds to its completion percentage. Sprint 1 shows ~80% filled, Sprint 2 shows ~37.5% filled, Sprint 3 shows 0% filled (empty bar).\n  1472→\n  1473→#### Test: Cycle list updates when a new cycle is created\n  1474→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles` with 2 existing cycles.\n  1475→- **Action**: User creates a new cycle \"Sprint 4\" via the \"New Cycle\" button.\n  1476→- **Expected**: The cycle list now shows 3 cycles, with \"Sprint 4\" appearing in the list with 0 issues and an empty progress bar.\n  1477→\n  1478→#### Test: Clicking a different cycle after viewing one switches the detail view\n  1479→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles` and has clicked \"Sprint 2\" to view its detail.\n  1480→- **Action**: User clicks back to the cycle list and clicks \"Sprint 1\".\n  1481→- **Expected**: The detail view updates to show \"Sprint 1\" cycle information (name, date range, stats, issues, burndown chart). No stale data from \"Sprint 2\" is shown.\n  1482→\n  1483→### CycleDetail\n  1484→\n  1485→#### Test: Cycle detail view renders cycle name and date range\n  1486→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles` and clicks on \"Sprint 2\" (Jan 15–Jan 28).\n  1487→- **Expected**: The detail view header displays the cycle name \"Sprint 2\" and the date range \"Jan 15 – Jan 28\" prominently at the top.\n  1488→\n  1489→#### Test: Cycle detail shows progress stats (total, completed, in progress, remaining)\n  1490→- **Initial state**: User views cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" which has 8 total issues: 3 done, 2 in progress, 3 remaining (backlog/todo).\n  1491→- **Expected**: Four progress stat cards/sections are displayed: \"Total: 8\", \"Completed: 3\", \"In Progress: 2\", \"Remaining: 3\". The stats are clearly labeled and visually distinct.\n  1492→\n  1493→#### Test: Cycle detail shows progress bar with correct completion percentage\n  1494→- **Initial state**: User views cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" with 3 of 8 issues completed (37.5%).\n  1495→- **Expected**: A progress bar is displayed showing approximately 37.5% completion. The percentage text \"37.5%\" (or \"3 of 8\") is visible near the progress bar.\n  1496→\n  1497→#### Test: Cycle detail displays filtered issue list matching Team Issues layout\n  1498→- **Initial state**: User views cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" which has 8 issues across various statuses and priorities.\n  1499→- **Expected**: An issue list is displayed below the progress stats using the same layout as the Team Issues page. Each issue row shows: priority icon, issue identifier (e.g., \"ENG-42\"), title (clickable), status icon, labels as colored badges, assignee avatar, due date, and project name. Issues are grouped by status by default.\n  1500→\n  1501→#### Test: Clicking an issue in cycle detail navigates to issue detail page\n  1502→- **Initial state**: User is viewing cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" with issue \"ENG-42\" visible.\n  1503→- **Action**: User clicks on the issue title \"ENG-42\".\n  1504→- **Expected**: User is navigated to `/issue/<issueId>` showing the full issue detail page for ENG-42.\n  1505→\n  1506→#### Test: Cycle detail issue list supports grouping by status, priority, assignee\n  1507→- **Initial state**: User is viewing cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" with 8 issues.\n  1508→- **Action**: User changes the \"Group by\" option from \"Status\" to \"Priority\".\n  1509→- **Expected**: Issues are regrouped by priority level (Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No Priority). Each group has a collapsible header showing the priority icon and name. Changing to \"Assignee\" regroups by assigned team member.\n  1510→\n  1511→#### Test: Cycle detail issue list supports sorting\n  1512→- **Initial state**: User is viewing cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" with issues grouped by status.\n  1513→- **Action**: User changes \"Sort by\" to \"Priority\".\n  1514→- **Expected**: Issues within each group are reordered by priority (Urgent first, then High, Medium, Low, No Priority).\n  1515→\n  1516→#### Test: Cycle detail issue list supports filtering\n  1517→- **Initial state**: User is viewing cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" with 8 issues. 2 issues have status \"Done\".\n  1518→- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects \"Done\" only.\n  1519→- **Expected**: The issue list shows only the 2 completed issues. Other issues are hidden. The filter is visually indicated as active.\n  1520→\n  1521→#### Test: Cycle detail issue list supports bulk actions\n  1522→- **Initial state**: User is viewing cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" with multiple issues.\n  1523→- **Action**: User selects checkboxes on 3 issues, then uses the bulk action to change status to \"In Progress\".\n  1524→- **Expected**: All 3 selected issues update their status to \"In Progress\". The progress stats update accordingly (e.g., \"In Progress\" count increases by 3). Checkboxes are deselected after the action.\n  1525→\n  1526→#### Test: Cycle detail progress stats update when an issue status changes\n  1527→- **Initial state**: User is viewing cycle detail for \"Sprint 2\" with 3 completed and 5 remaining issues.\n  1528→- **Action**: User changes one issue's status from \"Todo\" to \"Done\" via the status icon in the issue row.\n  1529→- **Expected**: The progress stats update to show \"Completed: 4\", \"Remaining: 4\". The progress bar updates to reflect 4/8 = 50% completion.\n  1530→\n  1531→#### Test: Cycle detail renders correctly for a cycle with no issues\n  1532→- **Initial state**: User views a newly created cycle \"Sprint 4\" that has no issues.\n  1533→- **Expected**: The progress stats show \"Total: 0\", \"Completed: 0\", \"In Progress: 0\", \"Remaining: 0\". The progress bar is empty (0%). The issue list shows an empty state message (e.g., \"No issues in this cycle\"). The burndown chart shows no data.\n  1534→\n  1535→### CreateCycle\n  1536→\n  1537→#### Test: \"New Cycle\" button is visible on the cycles page\n  1538→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, navigates to `/team/eng-1/cycles`.\n  1539→- **Expected**: A \"New Cycle\" button is visible on the page, styled consistently with other create buttons in the app (e.g., primary accent color, plus icon or text label \"New Cycle\").\n  1540→\n  1541→#### Test: Clicking \"New Cycle\" opens create cycle modal with correct fields\n  1542→- **Initial state**: User is on `/team/eng-1/cycles`.\n  1543→- **Action**: User clicks the \"New Cycle\" button.\n  1544→- **Expected**: A modal dialog opens with: a \"Name\" text input field (required), a \"Start date\" date picker, an \"End date\" date picker, a \"Create\" button, and a \"Cancel\" button. The modal has a title like \"New Cycle\" or \"Create Cycle\".\n  1545→\n  1546→#### Test: Successfully creating a cycle with all fields filled\n  1547→- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open. Team has no active cycle.\n  1548→- **Action**: User enters \"Sprint 5\" in the Name field, selects Feb 12 as Start date, selects Feb 25 as End date, and clicks \"Create\".\n  1549→- **Expected**: The modal closes. The cycle list now includes \"Sprint 5\" with the date range \"Feb 12 – Feb 25\", 0 issues, and an empty progress bar. The new cycle appears in the list.\n  1550→\n  1551→#### Test: Create cycle validates that name is required\n  1552→- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open.\n  1553→- **Action**: User leaves the Name field empty, sets start and end dates, and clicks \"Create\".\n  1554→- **Expected**: A validation error message appears near the Name field (e.g., \"Name is required\"). The modal remains open. No cycle is created.\n  1555→\n  1556→#### Test: Create cycle validates that end date is after start date\n  1557→- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open.\n  1558→- **Action**: User enters \"Sprint 5\" in Name, selects Feb 25 as Start date, selects Feb 12 as End date (before start), and clicks \"Create\".\n  1559→- **Expected**: A validation error message appears (e.g., \"End date must be after start date\"). The modal remains open. No cycle is created.\n  1560→\n  1561→#### Test: Create cycle validates start and end dates are required\n  1562→- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open.\n  1563→- **Action**: User enters \"Sprint 5\" in Name but does not set start or end dates, and clicks \"Create\".\n  1564→- **Expected**: Validation error messages appear for both date fields (e.g., \"Start date is required\", \"End date is required\"). The modal remains open. No cycle is created.\n  1565→\n  1566→#### Test: Cancel button closes the create cycle modal without creating\n  1567→- **Initial state**: Create cycle modal is open. User has entered \"Sprint 5\" in the Name field.\n  1568→- **Action**: User clicks \"Cancel\".\n  1569→- **Expected**: The modal closes. No new cycle is added to the cycle list. The form data is discarded."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019ZFhiq3FASdg1n41XBSME9","session_id":"1e17ab70-0a33-4d2a-af23-66b102e400e2","uuid":"80cfb1af-64b4-45f5-8f6e-79269093337f"}
