[2026-03-16T01:51:59.004Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GRSYAT3rR8QufRoAxpxNxy","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import type { Context } from '@netlify/functions';\n     2→import { getSql } from './db';\n     3→import crypto from 'crypto';\n     4→\n     5→function hashPassword(password: string, salt: string): string {\n     6→  return crypto.pbkdf2Sync(password, salt, 10000, 64, 'sha512').toString('hex');\n     7→}\n     8→\n     9→function generateToken(): string {\n    10→  return crypto.randomBytes(48).toString('hex');\n    11→}\n    12→\n    13→export default async function handler(req: Request, _context: Context) {\n    14→  if (req.method !== 'POST') {\n    15→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Method not allowed' }), {\n    16→      status: 405,\n    17→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    18→    });\n    19→  }\n    20→\n    21→  try {\n    22→    const { email, password } = await req.json();\n    23→\n    24→    if (!email || !password) {\n    25→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Email and password are required' }), {\n    26→        status: 400,\n    27→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    28→      });\n    29→    }\n    30→\n    31→    const sql = getSql();\n    32→    const users = await sql`SELECT id, name, email, password_hash, password_salt FROM members WHERE email = ${email}`;\n    33→    const user = users[0];\n    34→\n    35→    if (!user) {\n    36→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid email or password' }), {\n    37→        status: 401,\n    38→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    39→      });\n    40→    }\n    41→\n    42→    const hashedAttempt = hashPassword(password, user.password_salt);\n    43→    if (hashedAttempt !== user.password_hash) {\n    44→      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid email or password' }), {\n    45→        status: 401,\n    46→        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    47→      });\n    48→    }\n    49→\n    50→    const token = generateToken();\n    51→    const expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();\n    52→\n    53→    await sql`INSERT INTO sessions (token, member_id, expires_at) VALUES (${token}, ${user.id}, ${expiresAt})`;\n    54→\n    55→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({\n    56→      user: { id: user.id, name: user.name, email: user.email },\n    57→      token,\n    58→    }), {\n    59→      status: 200,\n    60→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    61→    });\n    62→  } catch (err) {\n    63→    console.error('Login error:', err);\n    64→    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Internal server error' }), {\n    65→      status: 500,\n    66→      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    67→    });\n    68→  }\n    69→}\n    70→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e17ab70-0a33-4d2a-af23-66b102e400e2","uuid":"ba4bb155-d3c4-4779-8b57-b6c62114fc66","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/login.ts","content":"import type { Context } from '@netlify/functions';\nimport { getSql } from './db';\nimport crypto from 'crypto';\n\nfunction hashPassword(password: string, salt: string): string {\n  return crypto.pbkdf2Sync(password, salt, 10000, 64, 'sha512').toString('hex');\n}\n\nfunction generateToken(): string {\n  return crypto.randomBytes(48).toString('hex');\n}\n\nexport default async function handler(req: Request, _context: Context) {\n  if (req.method !== 'POST') {\n    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Method not allowed' }), {\n      status: 405,\n      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    });\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const { email, password } = await req.json();\n\n    if (!email || !password) {\n      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Email and password are required' }), {\n        status: 400,\n        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n      });\n    }\n\n    const sql = getSql();\n    const users = await sql`SELECT id, name, email, password_hash, password_salt FROM members WHERE email = ${email}`;\n    const user = users[0];\n\n    if (!user) {\n      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid email or password' }), {\n        status: 401,\n        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n      });\n    }\n\n    const hashedAttempt = hashPassword(password, user.password_salt);\n    if (hashedAttempt !== user.password_hash) {\n      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid email or password' }), {\n        status: 401,\n        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n      });\n    }\n\n    const token = generateToken();\n    const expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + 30 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();\n\n    await sql`INSERT INTO sessions (token, member_id, expires_at) VALUES (${token}, ${user.id}, ${expiresAt})`;\n\n    return new Response(JSON.stringify({\n      user: { id: user.id, name: user.name, email: user.email },\n      token,\n    }), {\n      status: 200,\n      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    });\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error('Login error:', err);\n    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: 'Internal server error' }), {\n      status: 500,\n      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    });\n  }\n}\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":70}}}
[2026-03-16T01:52:21.577Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WVPWAS9VR9uMMdPHiAGHTT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `getSql()` creates a new Neon connection each time it's called. The `neon()` function from `@neondatabase/serverless` uses HTTP-based connections (not TCP), so connection pooling isn't an issue in the same way as traditional Postgres clients.\n\nHowever, each test makes multiple API calls:\n1. `loginViaApi` → POST /api/login (2 DB queries: SELECT + INSERT)\n2. `getTeams` → GET /api/teams (1+ DB queries)\n3. Plus browser-side API calls for loading the page\n\nAfter 5 tests, that's 15+ API calls with 30+ DB queries. The Neon ephemeral branch might be rate-limiting or the endpoint might become temporarily unavailable.\n \nActually, I'm reconsidering this. The dev server loads the function handlers at startup using `import()`, and each handler reads `process.env.DATABASE_URL`, so the ephemeral DB URL should be consistent across all calls. The real constraint might be Neon's free tier connection limit of 5 connections per endpoint—even though these are HTTP-based requests rather than persistent connections, they could still be hitting that ceiling when tests run in parallel.\n\nLooking at this more carefully, test 5 is marked as `test.slow()` and takes a long time, making multiple API requests for dropdowns and UI interactions. Once it finishes, the server might have accumulated pending requests or the Neon endpoint could be rate-limiting. But I should also check if the dev server is properly handling errors—if `handler(fnReq)` throws before responding, it might leave requests hanging. More fundamentally though, I'm wondering if the Neon endpoint is timing out or scaling to zero due to inactivity, since Neon's ephemeral branches have that auto-scaling behavior.\n\nThe real fix is probably to switch from bare `fetch` calls to `page.request` from Playwright, which operates through the browser context and is designed for API testing. This should be more reliable than Node.js fetch. I'm also noticing that other test files with the same pattern seem to pass, which makes me think the issue might be specific to how many tests are running or how the API calls are being made.\n\nActually, I'm wondering if there's a WebSocket connection issue with Vite's HMR—each new page opens a connection, and after many tests those might accumulate. But first, let me add better error logging to see what the login endpoint is actually returning when it fails.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_read_input_tokens":108480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":995,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e17ab70-0a33-4d2a-af23-66b102e400e2","uuid":"9d19e946-5750-4c10-a82f-d09ce2de606f"}
