[2026-03-16T01:56:44.424Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FAbcSnWgGeD7C83xQXNfsW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great progress! Now the results are much better. Let me analyze the failures:\n\n**Passed tests (9/14):**\n1. Create Issue button is visible and styled ✅\n2. Cancel button is visible ✅  \n3. Cancel button closes the modal ✅\n4. Cancel button discards form data ✅\n5. Create Issue button submits the form with all fields ✅ (labels dropdown fix worked!)\n6. Create Issue with only required fields ❌\n7. Created issue appears in the team issues list ❌\n8. Created issue with parent appears as sub-issue ❌\n9. Created issue generates activity history entry ❌\n\n\n10. Create Issue button is disabled during submission ✅\n11. Clicking outside the modal closes it ✅\n12. Pressing Escape closes the modal ✅\n13. Creating multiple issues in sequence works correctly ✅\n14. Created issue generates inbox notification for assignee ❌\n\nLooking at the 5 failures, the first one is interesting—test 6 created an issue under the Design team instead of Engineering, showing \"DES-4\" instead of \"ENG-\". The test opens the modal without navigating to the ENG team first, so it's defaulting to whatever team context is active. the Engineering team should be the default when opening the modal from that page. There might be a race condition where the `defaultTeamId` prop isn't passed or arrives late, causing the form to default to the first team in the list instead. Test 7 is failing because previous tests created extra issues, so the count is 9 instead of the expected 8. Test 8's parent search for \"Fix login\" came up empty, which could indicate another data or timing issue.\n\nThe core problems are data contamination between tests, the team selector defaulting incorrectly, and the search API not finding newly created issues. I need to add cleanup in `beforeEach` to remove non-seed issues, ensure the modal respects the current team context, and switch to relative assertions instead of hardcoded counts.\n\nLooking at test 6 more closely, the issue was created as \"DES-4\" when it should've been \"ENG-4\", which means the modal's team selector wasn't properly initialized to the ENG team even though we navigated there first. The helper functions navigate to the team page and click the new issue button, but something's going wrong with how the modal picks up the current team context.\n\nI'm wondering if the database state from earlier tests is affecting this—maybe a previous test left data that's interfering. Though Playwright gives each test a fresh page context, the database is shared across tests, so leftover data could be persisting and causing the team selector to default incorrectly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1479,"cache_read_input_tokens":117861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1479,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e17ab70-0a33-4d2a-af23-66b102e400e2","uuid":"fac59968-5433-4b4d-8f93-f395a7336cdd"}
