[2026-03-16T02:10:09.724Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked to fix failing tests in `tests/create-issue-modal-actions-integration.spec.ts` for the LinearClone app, following the skill file at `skills/tasks/build/testing.md`. The task is subtask \"FixTests: tests/create-issue-modal-actions-integration.spec.ts\". Once ALL subtasks are completed, output `<DONE>`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Playwright testing with Replay browser for recordings\n   - React 18 with Redux state management\n   - Neon ephemeral database branches for test isolation\n   - Custom dev-server.ts that proxies API to netlify functions and frontend to Vite\n   - Dropdown close behavior via mousedown event listeners\n   - React effect ordering (children before parents) and stale closures\n   - `test.describe.serial` for shared database state\n   - Relative count assertions vs hardcoded counts\n   - `toPass()` retry pattern for eventually consistent UI\n   - `loginViaApi` using Node.js `fetch` (not Playwright request)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/create-issue-modal-actions-integration.spec.ts`\n     - Main test file being fixed, 14 tests total\n     - Added retry logic to `loginViaApi` and `getTeams` helpers:\n     ```typescript\n     async function loginViaApi(baseURL: string, email: string, password: string) {\n       let lastError = '';\n       for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 5; attempt++) {\n         try {\n           const response = await fetch(`${baseURL}/api/login`, {\n             method: 'POST',\n             headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n             body: JSON.stringify({ email, password }),\n           });\n           const text = await response.text();\n           if (response.ok) {\n             const data = JSON.parse(text);\n             if (data.token) return data;\n           }\n           lastError = `status=${response.status} body=${text.slice(0, 200)}`;\n         } catch (e) {\n           lastError = `fetch error: ${e}`;\n         }\n         if (attempt < 4) await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 3000));\n       }\n       throw new Error(`loginViaApi failed after 5 attempts: ${lastError}`);\n     }\n     ```\n     - Changed `test.describe` to `test.describe.serial`\n     - Added team selector verification in \"required fields\" test\n     - Changed hardcoded count to relative count in \"appears in list\" test\n     - Added retry for search API in \"activity history\" test\n     - Added API verification + toPass retry for notification test\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueForm.tsx`\n     - Fixed dropdown close behavior - the outside-click handler now also closes dropdowns when clicking non-dropdown form elements:\n     ```typescript\n     useEffect(() => {\n       function handleClickOutside(e: MouseEvent) {\n         const target = e.target as HTMLElement;\n         if (formRef.current && !formRef.current.contains(target)) {\n           setOpenDropdown(null);\n           return;\n         }\n         if (!target.closest('.cif-dropdown-wrapper')) {\n           setOpenDropdown(null);\n         }\n       }\n       if (openDropdown) {\n         document.addEventListener('mousedown', handleClickOutside);\n       }\n       return () => document.removeEventListener('mousedown', handleClickOutside);\n     }, [openDropdown]);\n     ```\n\n   - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueModal.tsx`\n     - Fixed defaultTeamId prop to prioritize Redux state:\n     ```typescript\n     defaultTeamId={createIssueDefaultTeamId || params.teamId || workspace?.default_team_id || undefined}\n     ```\n     - Key insight: Modal is rendered outside `<Routes>` in App.tsx (line 51), so `useParams()` never has `teamId